summary is: {{ CC:

Back pain.

HPI:

Ms. Lee is a 40-year-old female who presents today for an evaluation of back pain. The patient states she was at a birthday party and was surprised and jumped up and fell down the stairs. She reports pain to the right side of her back. The pain is constant and worsens with twisting motions. She denies any pain down her legs.

EXAM

Examination of the spine shows limited range of motion with rotation. Neurologically, the patient has a normal sensation to light touch and pinprick bilaterally below the level of T4. Motor strength is 5/5 bilaterally in the lower extremities. Reflexes are 2+ and symmetric at the knees and ankles.

RESULTS

Lumbar spine x-ray obtained today shows prior hardware placement from a previous lumbar fusion.

ASSESSMENT

• Strain of muscle, fascia, and tendon of the back wall, subsequent encounter.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and radiographic findings today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regard to her current symptoms. I have advised her to continue taking ibuprofen 800 mg, 3 times a day with food. I have also advised her to use ice and heat alternately to her back and to walk. She will follow up with me in one week if her symptoms do not improve or worsen.

All questions were answered.
