Right knee pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Rebecca Johnson is a 27-year-old female who presents for an evaluation of right knee pain. The onset of her symptoms began approximately one month ago. She has been experiencing moderate pain in her right knee. The pain occurs after 2 laps of swimming and has been progressively worsening. She denies any trauma or injury to the knee. She has been swimming more regularly over the past month.

MEDICAL HISTORY

Patient reports a history of carpal tunnel release, status resolved. She also reports a history of chronic back pain and depression.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports she is a teacher. She has been swimming regularly over the past month.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports right knee pain.
Psychiatric: Reports depression, history of depression.
Neurological: Denies radicular symptoms.
General: Reports chronic back pain.

PHYSICAL EXAM

MSK: No swelling in the joints. Pain with patellar inhibition of the right knee. Normal range of motion of the right knee.
CV: Regular rate and rhythm.
