summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Hypertension and palpitations.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Jordan Roberts is a 49-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the management of hypertension. He was recently seen in the emergency room for elevated blood pressure and palpitations. The patient states he has a history of hypertension. He has been feeling fine and has not experienced any episodes of palpitations since his last visit.

The patient reports that he has had issues with hypertension since he was young. He states he has a family history of hypertension. He states he thought his blood pressure was better and he has a new primary care physician who placed him on a new medication one month ago.

The patient is currently taking Lisinopril 10 mg daily and Benicar HCT 20-5 mg daily. He is taking his blood pressure daily and reports his blood pressure has been running 146-155. He is trying to limit his salt intake and is trying to walk on the treadmill when he can.

GENDER

Male.

AGE

49.

DATE OF BIRTH

03/02/1972.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports he is married with two children. He is a truck driver and works night shifts. He is a college graduate and enjoys walking on the treadmill and playing video games.

FAMILY HISTORY

Positive for hypertension.

CURRENT MEDICATIONS

Lisinopril 10 mg daily.
Benicar HCT 20-5 mg daily.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Heart: Regular rate and rhythm.
Lungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally.

RESULTS

Potassium 4.0 mmol/L, 03/01/2021.

ASSESSMENT

Resistant hypertension.

PLAN

I have added spironolactone to his regimen. We will need to monitor his potassium and sodium. He will have a metabolic panel and blood pressure check in 2 weeks. Next medication would be carvedilol, which I would like to avoid giving, it's potential for erectile dysfunction. I have talked to the patient about that and the potential side effects of spironolactone, including the gynecomastia and electrolyte disturbances. If he is not controlled on spironolactone, the next step would be sending him to a resistant hypertension clinic.

INSTRUCTIONS

