summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Follow-up for rosacea.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Jacqueline Miller is a 32-year-old female who presents for follow-up for rosacea.

The patient reports that she has been using sulfacetamide wash twice daily and metronidazole cream after washing. She has also been using doxycycline 100 mg once daily for the past week. She has been taking doxycycline for the past 2 weeks, and she noticed improvement. However, she stopped breastfeeding and asked for doxycycline at that time. She has plateaued on improvement with the doxycycline once daily, so she started taking it twice daily again. She read that doxycycline could be problematic and stopped using the elidel cream. She has been using doxycycline once daily for the past week and is not breastfeeding.

The patient reports that she has fitzpatrick skin type IV-V. She has erythematous papules on her bilateral medial cheeks. There is mild erythema around and beneath her nostrils. She is using doxycycline twice daily and sulfacetamide wash twice daily. She is not using cetaphil cleanser, neutrogena wipes, or lotion. She is not using elidel cream.

The patient is advised to continue doxycycline twice daily until her rash is resolved, then once daily for another week before stopping. She is also advised to continue sulfacetamide wash once daily and metronidazole cream after washing.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Perioral dermatitis.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has plateaued on doxycycline once daily.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed that doxycycline is low risk. I advised that she continue doxycycline twice daily until her rash is resolved, then once daily for another week before stopping.
• Medical Treatment: Continue doxycycline 100 mg twice daily until the rash resolves, then once daily for another week before stopping. Continue sulfacetamide wash once daily. Continue metronidazole cream after washing.

2. Rosacea.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has been using sulfacetamide wash and metronidazole cream.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed that she should continue using sulfacetamide wash once daily. She can continue metronidazole cream after washing. I advised that she avoid any anti-aging or plant-based products. She should reach out if she tries any new products.
• Medical Treatment: Continue sulfacetamide wash once daily. Continue metronidazole cream after washing.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 4 weeks. She will reach out if she starts to flare. I will give her samples of vanicream.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
