ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Bobby Anderson is a 64-year-old male who presents with right upper quadrant abdominal pain. He has a history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and a family history of gallbladder disease. His abdominal ultrasound reveals multiple gallstones and mild inflammation of the gallbladder.

Cholecystitis with gallstones.
- Medical Reasoning: Given the patient's symptoms, physical exam findings, and imaging results, I believe the patient has mild cholecystitis with gallstones. He has not had any improvement with dietary modifications.
- Patient Education and Counseling: I discussed with the patient that the best course of action would be to remove his gallbladder. I explained that this procedure is called a laparoscopic cholecystectomy and it will take about 1 to 2 hours. The patient will spend the night in the hospital for observation.
